==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fr|en}} {{m|fr|vicereine}}, from {{m|en|vice-}} + {{m|en|reine||queen}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|en|/vʌɪsɹeɪn/|/ˈvʌɪsɹɛn/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# The wife of a [[viceroy]]. {{defdate|from 19th c.}}
#* '''1941''', {{w|W Somerset Maugham}}, ''Up at the Villa'', Vintage 2004, p. 19:
#*: ‘I can't imagine anything I'd like better than to be '''Vicereine''' of India,’ said the Princess.
# A woman who is a viceroy.

